  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal contract obligations in Vermont total $333M. Award activity shows 3,690 awards with an average award size of $90.3K. Obligations fell 62.0% year over year compared with the prior fiscal period. The largest single buyer so far is the Department of Defense with $205M in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $53M and the Department of Homeland Security with $36.4M. At the vendor level, GLOBALFOUNDRIES U.S. 2 LLC received $82.7M and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION received $46.3M. The largest industry by obligations is Semiconductor and Related Device Manufacturing at $82.7M, followed by Engineering Services at $54.3M and Other Computer Related Services at $35M. Historical annual obligations show fluctuations: FY21 $394M, FY22 $506M, FY23 $424M, FY24 $920M, FY25 $877M, and FY26 $333M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large are FY2026 to date obligations compared with recent years?",
        "body": "Obligations for FY2026 to date are $333M. That compares with FY25 $877M and FY24 $920M. Obligations were $424M in FY23, $506M in FY22, and $394M in FY21. Year over year obligations fell 62.0%."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors account for most federal spending in Vermont?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense accounts for the largest share with $205M in obligations. The next largest buyers are the Department of Veterans Affairs at $53M and the Department of Homeland Security at $36.4M. Major vendors include GLOBALFOUNDRIES U.S. 2 LLC at $82.7M and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $46.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
